### Basic Syntax (Elements and Attributes)

#### Place HTML parts at the matching brackets

<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;button class="button--external" style="border: 2px solid black;" disabled&gt;Click me&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('html-parts')} />

#### Indentation

Compare these three code snippets:

```html
<html><body><p>Why should I care about formatting?</p></body></html>
```

```html
<html>
<body>
<p>
Why should I care about formatting?
</p>
</body>
</html>
```

```html
<html>
	<body>
		<p>Why should I care about formatting?</p>
	</body>
</html>
```

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('html-indentation')} />

#### Closing tags and void elements

What goes wrong here?

```html
<img src="../img/icon.jpeg" alt="Icon"></img>
```

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('img-void-element')} />

What went wrong with these overlapping tags?

```html
<p>I didn't expect to find the <em>next-door neighbor's <strong>cat</em></strong> here!</p>
```

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('overlapping-tags')} />

